 ## Overview
-Volume Texture Mapping with ROI is a technique for rendering volumetric data by mapping a Data Region of Interest (ROI) within the source memory buffer to a Geometry ROI in world space, enabling the rendering of sub-volumes without copying data [S1]. It differs from full-volume rendering methods by allowing efficient access to specific data subsets via coordinate mapping and clipping, and from sparse methods by operating on dense grid textures managed by the OpenGL pipeline [S1].
+Volume Texture Mapping with ROI renders volumetric data by mapping a Data Region of Interest (ROI) within a source memory buffer to a Geometry ROI in world space, enabling sub-volume rendering without data copying [S1]. It differs from full-volume methods by restricting rendering to a specified data subset via coordinate mapping, and from sparse methods by operating on dense grid textures managed directly by the OpenGL pipeline [S1].
 
